  "label": "Cosplayer's current form is mapped as not being their final form",
  "description": "The text 'this isn't even my final form' is an analogical mapping that projects the visual material of the cosplayers (Goku and Luffy in their current cosplay forms) onto the textual concept of 'my final form'. The humor arises from the contrast between their current appearances and their iconic, powerful final forms in their respective anime series (Goku's Super Saiyan Blue and Luffy's Gear 5). The text explicitly states that their current state is not even close to their ultimate power level, creating a self-deprecating joke that relies on pop culture knowledge.",
